<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
   Auto Backup rules for API 30 and below. API 31+ uses data_extraction_rules.xml instead;
   both files must agree, because a device can restore under either.

   The only rule here is the session store, and it is a correctness rule before it is a
   security one:

   The refresh token in files/datastore/session.preferences_pb is encrypted with an
   AES key held in the Android Keystore. Keystore keys are device-bound and are NEVER
   included in a backup. So a restored copy of this file is ciphertext with no key –
   undecryptable by construction. Backing it up cannot restore a session; it can only put
   an encrypted credential somewhere it has no reason to be.

   `KeystoreTokenCipher.decrypt` handles the undecryptable case anyway (it returns null,
   the store clears itself, and the user signs in again), so this exclusion is the outer of
   two independent defences rather than the only one.

   Everything else – the Room cache and the receipt outbox – keeps the platform default
   of being backed up. Receipts are un-uploaded user data and are worth restoring.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude
        domain="file"
        path="datastore/session.preferences_pb" />
</full-backup-content>
